y5-compositor — building the Debian source package
=================================================

This is **Track B** (Ubuntu PPA, compile from source). It must not call
`compositor.installer/prepare.sh` or consume Track A `package.tar.gz`.
See `document/DISTRIBUTION.md`.

This package uses source format 3.0 (quilt). The upstream orig tarball
includes Cargo and npm vendored trees so Launchpad can build offline.

Creating a new orig tarball
---------------------------

Requirements on the maintainer machine (network allowed):

  - rustc/cargo via rustup stable (>= 1.95; Bevy MSRV — Ubuntu
    resolute's rustc 1.93 is too old, so the toolchain is bundled
    into the orig as rust-toolchain-dist/)
  - nodejs, npm, rsync, git, xz-utils

From a clean git checkout:

  debian/scripts/clean-tree.sh
  debian/scripts/make-orig.sh

This writes ../y5-compositor_<VERSION>.orig.tar.xz containing:

  - upstream sources (no debian/)
  - cargo-vendor/<component>/  (from cargo vendor --locked)
  - npm-vendor/logs-node_modules.tar.xz
  - rust-toolchain-dist/       (bundled rustc/cargo sysroot)

For local experiments with a dirty tree / existing vendor trees:

  debian/scripts/make-orig.sh --allow-dirty --reuse-vendor

Building
--------

  debuild -us -uc -b          # binary
  debuild -S -sa              # source (requires the orig above)

Do not ship debian/stage, target/, rustup, or cargo registries in the
source package. Use debian/scripts/clean-tree.sh before make-orig.

Important: debian/rules uses `dh_clean -X.orig` because the default
dh_clean deletes `*.orig`, which breaks `cargo-vendor/*/Cargo.toml.orig`
checksums.

Upload
------

  debian/upload-ppa.sh        # or: dput ppa:kacperpaczos/nourish …_source.changes
